otes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Idaho remains one of the most Republican states in the country, with a partisan lean of eighteen points to the right. No general-election polls of the state are available, no expert ratings have been published, and no fundraising or outside spending figures are reported, so expectations rest on the state's underlying partisanship. The incumbent president is term-limited, which removes any incumbency effect from the equation.\n\nNational headlines point to a competitive 2028 environment, with early primary polling showing JD Vance and Kamala Harris leading their parties and Republican donors split between Vance and Rubio. None of that changes Idaho's arithmetic: a generic Republican nominee begins with a lopsided advantage, and a Democratic win would require a national shift far beyond anything in the current evidence. The state is rated Safe Republican.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0246, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0539, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0537, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0553, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0476, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0546, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0466, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0509, "margin": -18.0}]}